      "content": "` tag. Removed the branch (3 lines) with Python.\n   - Bug 3: Advantage scaling (grpo_trainer.py:1090): `+ 1e4` should be `+ 1e-4`. Fixed with Edit.\n4. Verification:\n   - Ran the pre-fix verification script and confirmed all 3 bugs (sign inversion hypothesis True, got max = 7.18 > 0, \"no tag\" and \"prefix only\" were blanked out, max|adv| = 7.5e-05).\n   - Post-fix: re-ran the script — max|ref-got| = 0.0, got max = -2.31 ≤ 0, all degenerate shapes preserved, max|adv| = 1.5.\n   - Ran the skill's verify_pipeline.py — all invariants pass.\n   - Ran unit tests: 11 passed (decode/log_softmax/logprob/pad tests in test_utils.py).\n\nIncomplete / not verified:\n- I did not run the full GRPO trainer test suite (test_grpo_trainer.py) — I only ran the targeted utils tests.\n- I did not run an actual end-to-end training run to confirm model improvement (would require downloading the model, and the task was to fix the bugs).\n- I did not check every file in the TRL source for other potential bugs — I focused on the GRPO path (grpo_trainer.py, utils.py, grpo_config.py). I reviewed the generation phase, loss computation, and reference model handling, and they matched upstream. But a full audit of every file was not performed.\n\nLet me summarize clearly, distinguishing between completed and incomplete work.\n\nThe task states: \"The source code is in workspace/trl. Check whether there are bugs and fix them.\" So the main deliverable is finding and fixing bugs. I found and fixed 3 bugs, and verified them with numerical checks, the skill's verification script, and unit tests.\n\nLet me write a concise summary.\n</think>\n\n## Summary\n\nI found and fixed **3 bugs** in the GRPO training path under `workspace/trl`. I did not touch `train_grpo.py` or `reward_fn.py`.\n\n### Completed & verified\n\n**Bug 1 — Sign error in `selective_log_softmax`** (`trl/trainer/utils.py`)\nThe float32/float64 branch computed `logsumexp_values - selected_logits`, the *negative* of `log_softmax`. Log-probs came out positive (max ≈ +7.2), violating the `log_prob ≤ 0` invariant and corrupting the importance ratio and KL term in the loss.\n- Fixed to `selected_logits - logsumexp_values`.\n- Verified: now matches `F.log_softmax(...).gather(...)` exactly (max diff 0.0); max log-prob = −2.31 (≤ 0).\n\n**Bug 2 — `decode_and_strip_padding` blanked valid completions** (`trl/trainer/utils.py`)\nAn `else: text = \"\"` branch emptied any completion lacking a `</think>` tag (e.g. direct answers, truncated generations), so the reward function saw empty text → reward 0.0 → zero learning signal.\n- Removed the blanking branch; text is now preserved when the tag is absent (matches upstream and the existing unit-test contract).\n- Verified: \"no tags at all\" and \"only prefix\" cases now return their content instead of `''`.\n\n**Bug 3 — Advantage scaling constant** (`trl/trainer/grpo_trainer.py`, line 1090)\n`advantages / (std_grouped_rewards + 1e4)` divided advantages by ~10⁴, shrinking the policy-gradient signal to ~10⁻⁴ of intended (max|adv| ≈ 7.5e-05).\n- Fixed to `+ 1e-4` (upstream value).\n- Verified: max|adv| now 1.5.\n\n**Cross-checks that passed**\n- Skill's `verify_pipeline.py`: all invariants green (log-probs non-positive, match `F.log_softmax` to float32 tolerance, dominant-token ≈ 0, no non-empty decode becomes empty).\n- `tests/test_utils.py` (decode / log_softmax / logprob / pad): **11 passed**.\n\n### Incomplete / not verified\n- I did **not** run the full `test_grpo_trainer.py` suite or an end-to-end training run, so I have not empirically confirmed reward/loss curves improve over steps — only that each bug is fixed and the affected invariants hold.\n- I audited the GRPO path (`grpo_trainer.py`, `utils.py`, `grpo_config.py`); config defaults, generation, loss, and reference-model handling matched upstream. I did not exhaustively audit every other file in the package.\n\nIf you'd like, I can run the full GRPO trainer test suite next to close out the remaining verification.",
