_softmax`. Log-probs came out positive (max ≈ +7.2), violating the `log_prob ≤ 0` invariant and corrupting the importance ratio and KL term in the loss.\n- Fixed to `selected_logits - logsumexp_values`.\n- Verified: now matches `F.log_softmax(...).gather(...)` exactly (max diff 0.0); max log-prob = −2.31 (≤ 0).\n\n**Bug 2 — `decode_and_strip_padding` blanked valid completions** (`trl/trainer/utils.py`)\nAn `else: text = \"\"` branch emptied any completion lacking a `</think>` tag (e.g. direct answers, truncated generations), so the reward function saw empty text → reward 0.0 → zero learning signal.\n- Removed the blanking branch; text is now preserved when the tag is absent (matches upstream and the existing unit-test contract).\n- Verified: \"no tags at all\" and \"only prefix\" cases now return their content instead of `''`.\n\n**Bug 3 — Advantage scaling constant** (`trl/trainer/grpo_trainer.py`, line 1090)\n`advantages / (std_grouped_rewards + 1e4)` divided advantages by ~10⁴, shrinking the policy-gradient signal to ~10⁻⁴ of intended (max|adv| ≈ 7.5e-05).\n- Fixed to `+ 1e-4` (upstream value).\n- Verified: max|adv| now 1.5.\n\n**Cross-checks that passed**\n- Skill's `verify_pipeline.py`: all invariants green (log-probs non-positive, match `F.log_softmax` to float32 tolerance, dominant-token ≈ 0, no non-empty decode becomes empty).\n- `tests/test_utils.py` (decode / log_softmax / logprob / pad): **11 passed**.\n\n### Incomplete / not verified\n- I did **not** run the full `test_grpo_trainer.py` suite or an end-to-end training run, so I have not empirically confirmed reward/loss curves improve over steps — only that each bug is fixed and the affected invariants hold.\n- I audited the GRPO path (`grpo_trainer.py`, `utils.py`, `grpo_config.py`); config defaults, generation, loss, and reference-model handling matched upstream. I did not exhaustively audit every other file in the package.\n\nIf you'd like, I can run the full GRPO trainer test suite next to close out the remaining verification.",
